  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(1.2\\times0.5=0.6\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Take one half\n\nBecause \\(0.5\\) is one half, multiplying by \\(0.5\\) takes half of the other factor. The number \\(1.2\\) is \\(12\\) tenths, and half of \\(12\\) tenths is \\(6\\) tenths. Therefore, \\(1.2\\times0.5=0.6\\).",
